<article class="env-lemma" id="04Q3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04Q3">Lemma <span data-tag="04Q3">39.17.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. Let $p \in U \times _ S U$ be a point. Denote $R_ p$ the scheme theoretic fibre of $j = (t, s) : R \to U \times _ S U$. If $R_ p \not= \emptyset $, then the action </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  G_{0, \kappa (p)} \times _{\kappa (p)} R_ p \longrightarrow R_ p  \]
</div>
  <p> (see Lemma <a href="/tag/04Q2" data-tag="04Q2">39.17.4</a>) which turns $R_ p$ into a $G_{\kappa (p)}$-torsor over $\kappa (p)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The action is a pseudo-torsor by the lemma cited in the statement. And if $R_ p$ is not the empty scheme, then $\{ R_ p \to p\} $ is an fpqc covering which trivializes the pseudo-torsor. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>